\subsection{The knowledge part}

The knowledge part consists of questions from the course's example
exam, translated into English and lightly improved
(\cref{prior-knowledge,inventory-discussion}); unlike the concept
inventories, they may be shown here in full---that transparency is part
of why they were chosen.
The example exam groups its questions by topic; we selected one
question per group, so that the knowledge part spans the course's
intended learning outcomes---naming, control structures, usable
interaction, files, error handling, classes, and dividing programs into
functions---while staying short enough to sit alongside the R-SPQ-2F
and the background items.
The improvements are slight: a typo fixed, a doubled question reduced
to one.
Each item keeps the example exam's correct answer, but not its points:
the exam's growing point values implement its grading scheme, whereas
we measure knowledge by counting correct answers, so all items weigh
one point.
(The result view of \cref{app:quiz} still hides correctness from the
students.)

The items are numbered from position 11, so that their placement is
independent of the quiz they appear in: Canvas orders by position, gaps
are fine, and the numbering leaves room for quiz-specific items before
them, such as the end quiz's preparation item.

